<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL - Intel up, airlines quiet.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL - Intel up, airlines quiet.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intel Corp shares firmed preceding Wednesday's market open on news of a SoundView Financial &quot;buy&quot; reiteration and target price increase to $150 per share, traders said.</p>
<p>SoundView also raised its earnings outlook for the chip company.</p>
<p>Ahead of the opening bell, Intel was among the most active issues, rising to 126-3/4 from 125-7/8.</p>
<p>Traders said there were no trades in Delta Air Lines or Continental Airlines after media reports said they were negotiating Delta's acquisition of Continental.</p>
</text>
